) male song sparrows. Martingale residuals of a null model adjusting for hatch year are shown, smoothed using a cubic spline.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="rspb20070961f02"/></fig><fig id="fig3" position="float"><label>Figure 3</label><caption><p>Age-specific variation in reproductive value in (<italic>a</italic>) female and (<italic>b</italic>) male song sparrows. Values were calculated separately for each of 30 cohorts. Boxes, 25th, 50th (median) and 75th percentiles; dots, the means; lines, the full range of values.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="rspb20070961f03"/></fig><table-wrap id="tbl1" position="float"><label>Table 1</label><caption><p>Models relating ARS to age, inbreeding coefficients (<italic>f</italic>) and kinship coefficient (<italic>k</italic>) in female and male song sparrows. (<italic>F</italic> and <italic>R</italic> indicate the full dataset and restricted dataset of individuals that lived 4&#x02013;6 years, respectively. <italic>N</italic><sub>ind</sub> and <italic>N</italic><sub>obs</sub> are the sample sizes of individuals and observations, respectively. Individual <italic>f</italic> and mate <italic>f</italic> are the inbreeding coefficients of focal individuals and their mates, respectively. Sample sizes were reduced in analyses including <italic>f</italic> because individuals with unknown parents or grandparents were excluded. &#x02018;Individual&#x02019; and &#x02018;year&#x02019; represent the estimates of the variance components associated with the two random effects.)</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr><th valign="bottom" rowspan="3" align="left" colspan="1">dataset</th><th valign="bottom" rowspan="3" colspan="1"><italic>N</italic><sub>ind</sub></th><th valign="bottom" rowspan="3" colspan="1"><italic>N</italic><sub>obs</sub></th><th valign="bottom" colspan="2" align="left" rowspan="1">age</th><th valign="bottom" colspan="2" align="left" rowspan="1">age<sup>2</sup></th><th valign="bottom" colspan="2" alig